# The contact-page form, the lead popup and the WhatsApp chat all post to
# /api/lead, which forwards submissions to your app / CRM.
# These stay server-only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix) so the key never reaches the browser.
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in your CRM's details. Restart `npm run dev` after adding it.

# Performo's public lead-intake endpoint for this company (Bilal Shafqat
# Digital), e.g. https://performo.vercel.app/api/public/submissions
CRM_LEAD_API_URL=

# Sent as the x-api-key header (Performo's contract, not Authorization:
# Bearer) — from Company Settings -> Website Lead Capture Integration
# in Performo, logged in as Bilal Shafqat Digital.
CRM_LEAD_API_KEY=

# Field names sent to CRM_LEAD_API_URL (JSON POST), mapped in
# src/app/api/lead/route.ts to match Performo's /api/public/submissions:
#   type ("form" or "chat"), name, email, phone, message, service, campaign,
#   pageUrl, utmSource, utmMedium, utmCampaign, utmContent, utmTerm
# `source` (contact-page-form / whatsapp-chat / whatsapp-chat-skip) decides
# whether `type` is "form" or "chat".

# --- Lead backup when Performo is down (optional, server-only) ---
# If CRM_LEAD_API_URL is unset, rejects the lead, or cannot be reached, the
# visitor is still offered WhatsApp and email, and the route also:
#   1. appends the full lead as one JSON line to
#      ${LEAD_BACKUP_DIR}/failed-leads.jsonl (directory 0700, file 0600), and
#   2. emails the full lead to LEAD_ALERT_EMAIL, if SMTP is set below.
# Re-send saved leads once Performo is back:  npm run replay-leads
# (add `-- --dry-run` to preview). Delivered ones move to
# failed-leads.replayed.jsonl.
#
# PERSONAL DATA (UAE PDPL): these files hold names, emails, phones and messages
# in full. Keep the directory OUTSIDE the app folder and the web root (a path
# inside the app is refused), and delete the files once the leads are in
# Performo. Unset means ~/lead-backup for the account running Node.
LEAD_BACKUP_DIR=

# The file is still written past 5 MB, with a warning in the log on every
# write: at that size Performo has been failing for a long time.
#
# Who gets the alert email. Default bilal@bilalshafqat.com. At most one alert
# per 10 minutes; when many leads fail at once the next alert says how many
# were skipped (they are in the backup file).
LEAD_ALERT_EMAIL=
# Sender address. Default SMTP_USER. Must be a mailbox SMTP_USER may send as.
LEAD_ALERT_FROM=

# SMTP for the alert. bilalshafqat.com mail is Titan (Hostinger's email,
# MX mx1.titan.email): smtp.titan.email, port 465 (SSL). SMTP_USER is the full
# address, SMTP_PASS that mailbox's password. A dedicated mailbox (e.g.
# alerts@) is better than the main login if the plan allows a second one.
# Unset host, user or password means no email, with a line in the log.
SMTP_HOST=
SMTP_PORT=465
SMTP_USER=
SMTP_PASS=

# Proves a request came through Cloudflare (see clientIp in api/lead/route.ts).
# Any long random string; the same value goes in a Cloudflare Transform Rule
# that sets the request header x-origin-auth. Unset = previous behaviour.
# Set, a request without the right header is treated as a direct hit on the
# origin: cf-connecting-ip and x-real-ip are ignored and only the last
# X-Forwarded-For entry is used for rate limiting.
CF_ORIGIN_SECRET=

# --- Cloudflare Turnstile (optional bot check on the lead forms) ---
# Enforced ONLY when BOTH keys are set. The site key makes the forms render the
# (normally invisible) widget and send a token; the secret lets /api/lead verify
# it. Either one alone changes nothing, so a half-done setup cannot block leads.
# Create both in Cloudflare > Turnstile, widget mode "Managed" or "Invisible",
# hostname bilalshafqat.com.
#
# REBUILD after setting or changing the site key. NEXT_PUBLIC_ is baked into the
# build, and enforcement follows the BUILD (TURNSTILE_ENABLED_AT_BUILD in
# next.config.ts), not the runtime value. Setting both keys on Hostinger and
# only restarting changes nothing until the next `npm run build`; that is
# deliberate, because a route demanding tokens from forms built without the
# widget refused every lead.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# --- Content-Security-Policy reports (nothing to set) ---
# The CSP is report-only (next.config.ts). Browsers post violations to
# /api/csp-report, which logs one line per violation as
#   [CSP] directive=... blocked=<origin> page=<path>
# Read those in the Hostinger log for a week before switching the CSP to
# enforcing. No query strings or personal data are logged.

# --- Analytics (optional; nothing loads without it) ---
# Google Tag Manager container ID, e.g. GTM-XXXXXXX. NEXT_PUBLIC_ because it has
# to run in the browser. Put GA4, the Meta pixel, LinkedIn and TikTok tags INSIDE
# the container — that way new tracking never needs a code change or redeploy.
#
# The site pushes these events to the dataLayer for you to build triggers on:
#   generate_lead   — a lead confirmed as delivered to Performo.
#                     params: lead_source (contact-page-form | website-popup |
#                     whatsapp-chat), lead_service
#   whatsapp_click  — an outbound WhatsApp click.
#                     params: whatsapp_context
#
# Consent Mode v2 is wired up: all storage defaults to "denied" and flips to
# "granted" only when the visitor accepts the cookie banner.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GTM_ID=

# GA4 measurement ID, e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX. Loaded directly alongside GTM.
# A production build without GA4 or GTM prints a warning (next.config.ts).
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA4_ID=

# Meta Pixel ID. Fires only on bilalshafqat.com, never on localhost or previews.
# Unset, the production default in src/components/MetaPixel.tsx is used.
NEXT_PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID=

# --- Google Search Console (optional) ---
# Search Console > Settings > Ownership verification > HTML tag.
# Copy ONLY the token from content="..." , not the whole tag.
# Set this on Hostinger too, or the tag will be missing in production.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# --- Bing Webmaster Tools (optional) ---
# Bing > Settings > Verify ownership > "Meta tag". Copy ONLY the content value.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BING_SITE_VERIFICATION=

# --- IndexNow ---
# Already generated and committed as public/cfc44ddc83791ced09cff999b9915876.txt.
# Change both together if it is ever rotated.
INDEXNOW_KEY=cfc44ddc83791ced09cff999b9915876

# --- Booking (Cal.com) ---
# The event-type path only, no domain and no leading slash: "bilalshafqat/30min".
#
# Unset, /appointment falls back to collecting a time preference from a
# generated 09:00-17:30 grid that knows nothing about the real calendar, so a
# chosen slot is a request confirmed by hand. Set, the page embeds Cal.com and
# takes a real booking against live availability, and the "requested rather
# than booked" disclaimer disappears with the flow it belonged to.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ because the embed runs in the browser. There is no secret here:
# the booking page is public either way.
#
# Set this on Hostinger too, or production keeps the old request flow while
# local development takes real bookings.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CALCOM_LINK=
